  "finalReply": "Created `/app/image_analysis.py` with `load_image(image_folder, save_folder)` mirroring `/protected/loadimage.m`:\n\n- Finds files via `*.tif` in `image_folder` (sorted), raising `FileNotFoundError` if none — matching MATLAB's `dir` + `error`.\n- Reads each with PIL (`Image.open`, first frame only — matching `imread` default) to a numpy array.\n- Combines with MATLAB `cat(3, ...)` semantics: single file kept as-is (2-D stays 2-D); multiple files concatenated along axis 2, treating 2-D `(H,W)` as `(H,W,1)` so N grayscale images give `(H,W,N)`.\n- Creates `save_folder` if needed and saves as `I.npy` via `np.save`.\n\nSyntax verified with `py_compile`.",
